%p.mb-3
  Download the
  = link_to('quick_jump.js file', '/javascripts/widgets/quick_jump.js', rel: 'nofollow', class: 'fw-bold')
  and put it on your server.

%p.mb-3
  Paste this code into your HTML page where you want the Jump To widget to appear:

%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code
    = preserve do
      :escaped
        <div id="bp_quick_jump"></div>
        <script type="text/javascript">
          var BP_ontology_id = "#{@ontology.acronym}";
        </script>
        <script src="quick_jump.js" type="text/javascript" charset="utf-8"></script>

%p.mb-3
  This example assumes
  %code quick_jump.js
  is in the same folder as your HTML page. If you save it elsewhere, update the script's
  %code src
  path.

%h6.mt-4 Search multiple ontologies
%p.mb-3
  Replace the
  %code BP_ontology_id
  assignment with a comma-separated list of ontology IDs:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code var BP_ontology_id = "NCIT,SNOMEDCT";
%p.mb-3
  Or search all ontologies in #{$SITE}:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code var BP_ontology_id = "all";

%h6.mt-4 Include definitions
%p.mb-3
  To show definitions in the Jump To drop-down, add this line inside the configuration
  %code= '<script>'
  block, before loading
  = succeed ':' do
    %code quick_jump.js
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code var BP_include_definitions = true;

%p.mb-0
  For more help visit the
  = succeed '.' do
    = link_to('NCBO Wiki', 'https://www.bioontology.org/wiki/NCBO_Widgets#Ontology_search_widget', target: '_blank')
